From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:47:33 +0800
Subject: power: supply: preserve Piano power-off charging requests

Mark only the stock charger power_off_mode field before a connected
power-off. The original bootloader otherwise treats USB wakeup as a
normal Android boot. Keep restart and unplugged shutdown unchanged.

Resolve the unique internal-UFS GPT partition, validate the stock format,
and preserve every other byte through one logical-block read-modify-write.
Flush and compare the complete block on readback before device shutdown.

Exercise the real transaction with UML KUnit, including adjacent data,
busy storage, unplugging, repeated requests and I/O failures.

Require a connected UCSI sink and confirm VBUS and OTG with fresh ADSP replies. The field at v2 wire ID 0x21020 is CID; it can be zero with an active USB source.

Verify the live ADSP sink role after the VBUS, OTG and UCSI checks.

Keep the shared UCSI source check available when this power-off path
starts calling it. The helper comes from the USB overtemperature
support used later in the series.

Link: https://github.com/slwyts/Project-SunUEFI/commit/3d0bb37186d80c98cd9e99f67e0e1b9131bea6ad
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia@gmail.com>
Co-developed-by: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Signed-off-by: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
